A||N||6||Tonker||Oil pressure just jumped to max on me.||||5||
Z||000000||Tonker||09-04-2001||12:53 AM||||I was just outside to move my car from one side of the driveway to the other. Started up fine, but I noticed that the oil pressure guage is right off the scale!! It's been fine up until now. Any thoughts on how I can check if it's driveable, or should I just call a tow truck before I risk serious damage?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Black '86 Fiero GT.<BR>ICQ: 7813479||||reg||5
Z||000001||JetroGT||09-04-2001||01:50 AM||||It's probably just the sending unit. When it starts to go bad the gauge get jumpy then eventually pegs. It will also peg if it's unplugged.<P>I posted this a few weeks ago.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012763.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012763.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by JetroGT (edited 09-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tonker||09-04-2001||11:34 AM||||Is the car driveable, assuming that it's the sending unit?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero_24||09-04-2001||11:40 AM||||Watch out!  My car started doing that and I relaced the oil pressure sending unit, which was not the problem.  I thought it was reading wrong, but it wasn't.  The next day I lost all my oil pressure.  I can only hold oil pressure now for 20 minutes with 20W-50 weight oil.  I have no idea what the problem is (not the oil pump, I checked that already).  You may not have the same problem, but I am just passing info from my own personal experience.  <P>Craig<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||4
Z||000004||Tonker||09-04-2001||12:40 PM||||What does the oil sending unit do? Is there any way aside from replacing it that I use to tell if it's the problem?||||reg||1
Z||000005||varnster||09-04-2001||08:23 PM||||The sending unit is another satanic ploy by<BR>pontiac, It makes the owner of said car, rave<BR>like a freaking lunitic each time the car is started, I think a hula girl glued to the dash can predict whats going on with your engine just as well! I replaced the sending unit and it works {I guess} but I DONT TRUST<BR>IT, but it looks cool, and isnt that what we really want in the end.||||reg||12
Z||000006||Tonker||09-04-2001||11:09 PM||||Well, I just replaced my oil sending unit and in so doing made my first small skin sacrifice to the God of Fiero Engines. Thanks JetroGT for the instructions.. you might have mentioned something about the black clip on the plug that was designed by Lucifer himself...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Just trying to get that damn thing off took nearly 3/4 of the replacement time.<P>Anyways, thanks for the help guys!||||reg||10
